  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ExtensionObject_decodeBinary",
    "file": "open62541/src/ua_types_encoding_binary.c",
    "description": "The BYTESTRING ExtensionObject path mishandles ownership of a dynamically allocated non-numeric type NodeId. For an unknown type, ExtensionObject_decodeBinaryContent shallow-moves `*typeId` into `dst->content.encoded.typeId`; ExtensionObject_decodeBinary then unconditionally deletes the local `binTypeId` at line 947, leaving the destination ExtensionObject with a dangling NodeId string/ByteString pointer. If subsequent body decoding fails, Array_decodeBinary deletes the partially initialized ExtensionObject and frees that pointer again. The root fix must preserve single ownership (for example, do not delete `binTypeId` after the unknown-type transfer, or explicitly clear/move/copy it safely).",
    "conditions": "The harness selects UA_Variant (type index 0x0017). The payload encodes a Variant containing an array of one ExtensionObject (`0xd6`, length 1). That ExtensionObject has a dynamically allocated string NodeId (`0x03`, namespace 0x2020, one-byte identifier \" \") which cannot resolve to a known datatype, followed by BYTESTRING encoding (`0x01`) but no complete body length/content. The unknown-type path shallow-copies the NodeId into the destination; truncated body decoding returns an error after the local NodeId has been freed, and array error cleanup destroys the partially decoded element, causing the second free."
  },
